[al:新概念英语第二册]
[ti:66. Sweet as Honey]
[00:00.500]Passage 66 | 文章六十六
[00:02.420]Cycling through the air. | 空中骑行。
[00:06.090]The Hatfield Puffin is a modern aeroplane. | 赫特菲尔德海鹦号是一架现代飞机。
[00:10.850]But its designer, Mr. John Wimpenny, | 但它的设计师，约翰·温彭尼先生，
[00:14.030]is finding it difficult to get it off the ground. | 发现让它起飞很困难。
[00:18.140]The reason for this is that this plane is also a bicycle. | 原因是这架飞机也是一辆自行车。
[00:23.120]Its pilot has to pedal hard to get it into the air. | 它的飞行员必须努力蹬踏板才能让它升空。
[00:28.980]After Mr. Wimpenny had the plane built, | 温彭尼先生造好这架飞机后，
[00:32.865]it was tested thoroughly. | 它被彻底测试了。
[00:34.565]In 1961, | 1961年，
[00:37.570]it was the first man-powered aircraft to fly half a mile. | 它是第一架飞行了半英里的人力飞机。
[00:42.575]While being flown by a champion amateur cyclist in 1963, | 1963年，当它由一位业余自行车冠军驾驶时，
[00:48.540]the plane crashed on an airfield. | 这架飞机在机场坠毁了。
[00:51.600]Since then, Mr. Wimpenny has had it rebuilt. | 从那时起，温彭尼先生让人重建了它。
[00:55.880]He has had the length of the wings increased, | 他让人加长了机翼的长度，
[00:59.285]so that they now measure 93 feet. | 使它们现在测量为93英尺。
[01:02.265]Almost as long as those of a Dakota. | 几乎和达科他飞机的机翼一样长。
[01:05.935]Many people have shown interest in this new and unusual sport. | 许多人对这项新奇而不寻常的运动表现出了兴趣。
[01:11.445]But though air cyclists may learn how to fly over short distances, | 但是，尽管空中骑行者可能学会短距离飞行，
[01:16.385]and may eventually even get across the English Channel, | 甚至可能最终飞越英吉利海峡，
[01:20.880]it is doubtful whether they will ever cycle across the Atlantic. | 但他们是否能骑自行车横渡大西洋，这是令人怀疑的。